TI  - “Still in the Loop”: Coping with Technostress in DevOps Teams and the Impact of GenAI
AU  - Jeyam, Dharneeka
AU  - Wiedemann, Anna
AU  - Schwabe, Gerhard
AU  - Güney, Kadircan
T3  - ICSE-SEIP '26
AB  - The increasing adoption of generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) tools and evolving technologies in DevOps environments introduces novel stressors, known as technostress. In this qualitative study, we conducted 26 semi-structured interviews with DevOps team members to explore how technostress is experienced and managed in practice. Using inductive and deductive thematic analysis, we identified coping strategies that operate across multiple levels. Participants reported both emotion-focused and problem-focused coping strategies, including skill development, knowledge sharing, and tool standardization. While GenAI tools are valued for enhancing productivity and efficiency, they also introduce new stressors, such as hallucinations and unreliable output. Our findings highlight a dual role of GenAI, as both novel stressor and a potential mitigator. This duality underscores the ongoing responsibility of DevOps members to “still be in the loop” when integrating GenAI tools. Based on these insights, we propose a conceptual framework and offer actionable, multi-level coping strategies that extend beyond individual practices to organizational and tool-level measures, capturing how the integration of GenAI reshapes technostress in modern DevOps practices.
